{{define "main"}}
    {{- /* RG-3. Restoring destroys nothing -- the checkbook that is here is kept
           and named -- but it does replace every record in front of the
           household, in every tab they have open, with the ones from another
           day. The page says exactly what will happen and offers a way out. */ -}}
    <div class="register-head">
        <h1>Restore the backup taken {{.Chosen.Taken}}?</h1>
    </div>

    <dl class="problem-facts">
        <dt>Restore from</dt>
        <dd><code>{{.Chosen.Name}}</code></dd>
    </dl>
    <dl class="problem-facts">
        <dt>Replaces</dt>
        <dd><code>{{.Checkbook}}</code></dd>
    </dl>

    <p>
        This replaces the records in <code>{{.Checkbook}}</code> with the ones in
        <code>{{.Chosen.Name}}</code>. Anything entered since that backup was taken is not in it,
        and there is no way to merge the two.
    </p>
    <p>
        The checkbook you have now is kept, under a <code>checkbook-replaced-</code> name in the
        same folder, and the page you land on will say which. Nothing is deleted, and the backup
        itself is not altered.
    </p>
    <p class="muted">
        Any other window you have open on this checkbook will show the restored records the next
        time you use it.
    </p>

    <form method="post" action="/checkbook/restore">
        {{- /* The generation of the checkbook this page was drawn for, so a tab
               that has been on screen since before a swap is refused rather than
               applied to a database it was never looking at (CO-3). */ -}}
        <input type="hidden" name="generation" value="{{.Generation}}">
        <input type="hidden" name="path" value="{{.Chosen.Path}}">
        <input type="hidden" name="return" value="{{.ReturnTo}}">
        <div class="entry-fields">
            <div class="f-add"><button type="submit">Restore it</button></div>
            <div class="f-add"><a class="cta" href="/checkbook/restore">Keep what I have</a></div>
        </div>
    </form>
{{end}}
